   ],
   "textLength": 739,
   "text": "A few years ago, when Stacia Bourne and her husband would talk about having a second child, the conversation often turned to money.\n\"We were thinking we couldn't afford it,\" said Bourne, a University of Delaware psychology professor who lives in Maryland.\nTheir first child, George, was born in 2020 and started daycare when he was 2. \"The cost for childcare for him is about the same as our mortgage",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 4,
