   "textLength": 669,
   "text": "One of those grandparents is Jerry Larkin, 66, a former machinist who moved in with his daughter's family in Tulsa, Okla., during the COVID-19 pandemic to help take care of his twin grandsons, one of whom requires additional medical care.\nLarkin said he used to think he was alone in devoting so much time to caregiving, until he learned through social media and elsewhere that many families struggle",
